sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "By using an architecture akin to a variational autoencoder, in which the genome is a compressed generative representation decoded by the developmental layer, evolution is kept from over-training on past conditions and is pushed to produce general-purpose problem-solving organisms that display robustness, plasticity and adaptive success in entirely novel circumstances.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A generative, compressed genome pushes evolution toward general-purpose problem solvers";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Darwin's agential materials: evolutionary implications of multiscale competency in developmental biology”, Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS (2023), doi:10.1007/s00018-023-04790-z; section “Intelligence and evolution: the impact of competency at new scales”. Scope: Evolution of multicellular organisms"
}
